p.src:
The numbers should be preserved with the speaker’s uncertainty: $\begin{aligned}
\text{claimed giveaway} &= \$10{,}000, \\
\text{claimed closed business} &\approx \$100{,}000.
\end{aligned}$ The rough gross comparison is $\frac{\$100{,}000}{\$10{,}000}\approx 10.$ This is not net profit, audited return, or a promise that any referral offer produces the same result. It is an anecdotal gross multiple. The mechanism is the important part: $\begin{aligned}
\text{clear referral offer}
&+ \text{local attention} \\
&+ \text{credible incentive} \\
&\longrightarrow \text{introductions} \\
&\longrightarrow \text{closed business}.
\end{aligned}$

